HiGHS 1.15.1 as Cadpole builds it: everything linked in, nothing loaded, no CUDA,
no zlib. highs_module.patch is the MODULE.bazel half.

The BCR module as published does three things Cadpole cannot ship:

1. It defines HIGHS_SHARED_EXTRAS_LIBRARY (highs/HConfig.h.bazel.in) without
   building the extras library. HiGHS then dlopen()s "libhighs_extras.so"
   ("libhighs_extras.dylib" next to the binary on macOS) the first time it asks
   whether HiPO is available -- which every MIP's analytic-centre step and
   every option check does -- and uses HiPO's orderings if one is found. What a
   solve computes would then depend on which shared library the machine
   happens to have, and the binary would load code nobody linked. Here the two
   extras files are compiled into the library itself and HIGHS_SHARED_EXTRAS_
   LIBRARY is left undefined, which is HiGHS's own static mode
   (BUILD_SHARED_EXTRAS_LIB=OFF). HIPO stays undefined, so amd, metis, rcm and
   BLAS are neither compiled nor reachable: isAvailable<hipo>() is false on
   every machine and the IPM path is always IPX. HIGHS_EXTRAS_VERSION is what
   extern/CMakeLists.txt passes for that file.

2. It depends on rules_cuda 0.3.0 and calls its toolkit extension, which
   probes the host for a CUDA install at fetch time, and its BUILD loads
   cuda_library for a GPU PDLP that only a flag nobody sets would select.
   The dependency, the extension, the cuda_library and the config_setting
   that reads it are removed; CUPDLP_CPU is the only define. (Bazel applies a
   patch's MODULE.bazel hunk because Cadpole is the root module.)

3. It links @zlib, but HConfig.h.bazel.in never defines ZLIB_FOUND, so no
   HiGHS code calls zlib (only reading .mps.gz files would, and Cadpole passes
   models in memory). The dependency is removed, so the module graph keeps
   the zlib it had before HiGHS arrived and no zlib code reaches a binary.

Re-check all three when bumping HiGHS: compare the new BCR BUILD.bazel,
MODULE.bazel and highs/HConfig.h.bazel.in against this patch.

diff --git a/BUILD.bazel b/BUILD.bazel
--- a/BUILD.bazel
+++ b/BUILD.bazel
@@ -1,7 +1,5 @@
-load("@bazel_skylib//rules:common_settings.bzl", "bool_flag")
 load("@bazel_skylib//rules:copy_file.bzl", "copy_file")
 load("@rules_cc//cc:defs.bzl", "cc_binary", "cc_library", "cc_test")
-load("@rules_cuda//cuda:defs.bzl", "cuda_library", "requires_cuda")
 
 copy_file(
     name = "highs-config",
@@ -10,50 +8,23 @@ copy_file(
     visibility = ["//visibility:public"],
 )
 
-bool_flag(
-    name = "cupdlp_gpu",
-    build_setting_default = False,
-    visibility = ["//visibility:public"],
-)
-
-config_setting(
-    name = "cupdlp_gpu_enabled",
-    flag_values = {
-        "@rules_cuda//cuda:enable": "True",
-        "@local_cuda//:valid_toolchain_found": "True",
-        ":cupdlp_gpu": "True",
-    },
-)
-
 cc_library(
     name = "config",
     srcs = ["HConfig.h"],
     visibility = ["//visibility:public"],
 )
 
-cuda_library(
-    name = "cupdlp",
-    srcs = glob([
-        "highs/pdlp/cupdlp/cuda/*.cu",
-        "highs/pdlp/hipdlp/*.cu",
-    ]),
-    hdrs = glob([
-        "highs/pdlp/cupdlp/cuda/*.cuh",
-    ]),
-    defines = ["CUPDLP_GPU"],
-    target_compatible_with = requires_cuda(),
-    deps = [
-        "@local_cuda//:cublas",
-        "@local_cuda//:cusparse",
-    ],
-)
-
 cc_library(
     name = "highs",
     srcs = [
         "highs/interfaces/highs_c_api.cpp",
         "highs/HighsExternalApi.cpp",
         "highs/HighsExternalDeps.cpp",
+        # Cadpole: HiGHS's "extras" linked in, built without HiPO (no amd, metis,
+        # rcm or BLAS), so nothing is dlopen()ed at run time; see
+        # highs/HConfig.h.bazel.in.
+        "extern/HighsExtrasApi.cpp",
+        "extern/HighsExtrasExternalDeps.cpp",
     ] + glob([
         "highs/io/*.cpp",
         "highs/io/filereaderlp/*.cpp",
@@ -93,10 +64,8 @@ cc_library(
             "-Wno-unused-but-set-variable",
         ],
     }),
-    defines = select({
-        ":cupdlp_gpu_enabled": ["CUPDLP_GPU"],
-        "//conditions:default": ["CUPDLP_CPU"],
-    }),
+    defines = ["CUPDLP_CPU"],
+    local_defines = ['HIGHS_EXTRAS_VERSION=\\"1.15.1\\"'],
     includes = [
         "extern",
         "extern/catch",
@@ -125,13 +94,7 @@ cc_library(
         "//conditions:default": ["-lpthread"],
     }),
     visibility = ["//visibility:public"],
-    deps = [
-        "//:config",
-        "@zlib",
-    ] + select({
-        ":cupdlp_gpu_enabled": [":cupdlp"],
-        "//conditions:default": [],
-    }),
+    deps = ["//:config"],
 )
 
 cc_library(
